de-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=3\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{45}^{∘})\n$$" 13194139545674 17592186576411 true] [17592186406579 1074 "The difference formula for cosine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ &=3 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{1}{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =1 \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1) \\\\ ϕ & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={3}^{2}+(3)^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =2\\cdot {3}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2} & =18 \\\\ R & =3\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=3\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{45}^{∘})\n$$" 13194139545674 17592186576411 false] [17592186406755 1071 "What are the minimum and maximum of the set $A={-8,\\,0,\\,4,\\,-1}?$\n\n$\\min (A)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,\\max (A)=$\n{{field-2}}" 13194139545674 17592186576411 true] [17592186406755 1071 "What are the minimum and maximum of the set $A={-8,\\,0,\\,4,\\,-1}?$\n\n$min(A)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,max(A)=$\n{{field-2}}" 13194139545674 17592186576411 false] [17592186406755 1074 "Recall that \n\n- ${x}_{max}$ is the maximum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{max}\\in S$ and $x\\le {x}_{max}$ for all $x\\in S,$ and\n\n- ${x}_{min}$ is the minimum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{min}\\in S$ and ${x}_{min}\\le x$ for all $x\\in S.$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\min (A) & =\\min {-8,\\,0,\\,4,\\,-1}=-8 \\\\ \\max (A) & =\\max {-8,\\,0,\\,4,\\,-1}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139545674 17592186576411 true] [17592186406755 1074 "Recall that \n\n- ${x}_{max}$ is the maximum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{max}\\in S$ and $x\\le {x}_{max}$ for all $x\\in S,$ and\n\n- ${x}_{min}$ is the minimum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{min}\\in S$ and ${x}_{min}\\le x$ for all $x\\in S.$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}min(A) & =min{-8,\\,0,\\,4,\\,-1}=-8 \\\\ max(A) & =max{-8,\\,0,\\,4,\\,-1}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139545674 17592186576411 false] [17592186406757 1074 "Recall that \n\n- ${x}_{max}$ is the maximum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{max}\\in S$ and $x\\le {x}_{max}$ for all $x\\in S,$ and\n\n- ${x}_{min}$ is the minimum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{min}\\in S$ and ${x}_{min}\\le x$ for all $x\\in S.$\n\nNotice that $-2\\notin A$ and $1\\notin A.$ So, we have the following:\n\n- $\\min (A)=\\min (-2,1),$ which $\\text{does not exist}$\n\n- $\\max (A)=\\max (-2,1),$ which $\\text{does not exist}$" 13194139545674 17592186576411 true] [17592186406757 1074 "Recall that \n\n- ${x}_{max}$ is the maximum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{max}\\in S$ and $x\\le {x}_{max}$ for all $x\\in S,$ and\n\n- ${x}_{min}$ is the minimum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{min}\\in S$ and ${x}_{min}\\le x$ for all $x\\in S.$\n\nNotice that $-2\\